	(text "DAC: Ch A=Laser1 DC  Ch B=Laser2 DC  Ch C=TEC1  Ch D=TEC2  |  DDS f1=2.000kHz  f2=3.100kHz"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 13.462 20.494 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.2 1.2)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "17a6dc88-350d-4791-a412-54702310f0eb")
	)
	(text "REFERENCE DDS (per laser) - phase-adjustable demod LO  | \nEach laser has its OWN drive DDS (existing) + reference DDS (this block). \nChannels stay fully independent - each pair runs its own Omega (Omega_A != Omega_B).\nPHASE COHERENCE: all four AD9833 share the one 25 MHz Y_DDS via MCLK_REF. \nWithin a laser, drive+reference run identical frequency words, so after a SYNCHRONIZED RESET their phase accumulators stay locked. \nSet the demod phase with the reference DDS PHASE register; calibrate once in firmware against the error signal (drift-free, no analog trim).\nSPI: shared DDS_SCLK / DDS_SDATA bus; this DDS gets its OWN chip-select DDS3_FSYNC from a spare Teensy GPIO (SPI Mode 2, 3.3V - no level shift). \nVOUT -> LO1_REF -> AD831 LO (Mixer block).\nDecoupling C840=100n(VDD) C841=100n(CAP/2.5V) C842=10n(COMP) per datasheet - match your existing DDS decoupling. \n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 127.508 47.498 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "23cc1b63-0343-45d7-97aa-81be9672a385")
	)
